            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            does not reflect the existence of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            between homomorphsims/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            of groupoids (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidDependentlyTypes"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            is not what one is interested in when considering
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            In order to obtain the right notion of category of groupoids that does reflect homotopies, we first consider now the
            %em horizontal
            composition of homotopies/natural transformations.
