          %p
            For handling just groupoids exclusively their description in terms of Kan complexes may be a bit of an overkill, but the advantage is that it embeds groupoids naturally in the more general context of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groupoid"} 3-groupoid
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-functor"} pseudo-functor
            out of an ordinary groupoid into a 2-groupoid is simply a homomorphism of the corresponding Kan complexes.
          %p The disadvantage of the simplicial approach is the difficulty of describing multiple compositions in higher dimensions, an important idea which is quite conveniently handled cubically.
