          %p
          %h2#section_References References
          %p
            Apparently the earliest occurence of the concept of groupoids (see also
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brandt+groupoid"} Brandt groupoid
          %ul
            %li#Brandt27
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heinrich+Brandt"}> Heinrich Brandt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über eine Verallgemeinerung des Gruppenbegriffes
              %strong 96
              1 (1927) 360-366 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007%2FBF01209171"}> doi:10.1007/BF01209171
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further early discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+W.+Mackey"}> George W. Mackey
                , §11 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ergodic theory and virtual groups
                %strong 166
                (1966) 187–207 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01361167"}> doi:10.1007/BF01361167
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Higgins"}> Philip Higgins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Presentations of Groupoids, with Applications to Groups
                %strong 60
                (1964) 7-20 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100037397"}> doi;10.1017/S0305004100037397
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topologie Algébrique
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-49361-8"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-49361-8
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+J.+Higgins"}> Philip J. Higgins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and Groupoids
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 32
                %strong 7
                (2005) 1-195 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/7/tr7abs.html"}> tac:tr7
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/7/tr7-2a4.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A motivation and introduction of the concept of groupoid and a tour of examples (including the refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoids"} topological groupoids
            and
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupoids: Unifying Internal and External Symmetry – A Tour through some Examples
              %strong 43
              7 (1996) 744-752 &amp;lbrack;ams:notices/199607:
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/199607/weinstein.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Weinstein_Groupoids.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A textbook with an eye towards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            and) groupoids (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+representations"}> groupoid representations
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Ibort"}> Alberto Ibort
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miguel+A.+Rodriguez"} Miguel A. Rodriguez
              = succeed "," do
                %em An Introduction to Groups, Groupoids and Their Representations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.routledge.com/An-Introduction-to-Groups-Groupoids-and-Their-Representations/Ibort-Rodriguez/p/book/9781032086767?srsltid=AfmBOoqc0EH7Qjc1_0C-TYQtUbhTWpdb3Juy61vwE9TfRC5oaJwjlYfN"} ISBN:9781032086767
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/b22019"} doi:10.1201/b22019
          %p Further exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From groups to groupoids: A brief survey
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://pages.bangor.ac.uk/~mas010/gpdsweb.html"} Groupoids in Mathematics
                %strong 19
                2 (1987) 113-134 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/blms/19.2.113"}> doi:10.1112/blms/19.2.113
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://pages.bangor.ac.uk/~mas010/pdffiles/groupoidsurvey.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Alberto Santini,
                %em Topological groupoids
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://web.math.ku.dk/~moller/students/alberto.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Santini-Groupoids.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (about groupoids in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoids"} fundamental groupoids
                  – not about actual
                  = succeed "!)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoids"} topological groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Topology+--+2"} Introduction to Topology – 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Topology+--+2#Groupoid"} Groupoids
          %p
            With an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#Richter19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"}> Birgit Richter
              , Section 1.2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em From categories to homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108855891"} doi:10.1017/9781108855891
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/richter/catbook.html"} book webpage
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/richter/bookdraft.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology and groupoids
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://pages.bangor.ac.uk/~mas010/topgpds.html"} web
            %li#Zivaljevic
              %p
                Rade T. Živaljević,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupoids in combinatorics—applications of a theory of local symmetries
          %p
            Presenting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretorsion+theory"} pretorsion theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            whose torsion(-free) objects are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+categories"}> skeletal categories
            , respectively), hence whose “trivial objects” are the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+groupoids"} skeletal groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Federico+Campanini"} Federico Campanini
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marino+Gran"} Marino Gran
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
              %em
                Groupoids and skeletal categories form a pretorsion theory in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.08487"}> arXiv:2207.08487
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
